Subject: [PATCH] Restore original material registration order and destructor flow
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Restore eight constructors exactly to pinned source assignment/registration order.
Original game-module destructors retain the source empty bodies. Prior native
preview global/cache resets remain scoped to standalone diagnostics. No resource
selection, parameters, shader decisions or successful readiness are introduced.

diff --git a/src/NL/glx/GXCameraScrolledOverlayMaterialProgram.cpp b/src/NL/glx/GXCameraScrolledOverlayMaterialProgram.cpp
index 363f803..4c83e63 100644
--- a/src/NL/glx/GXCameraScrolledOverlayMaterialProgram.cpp
+++ b/src/NL/glx/GXCameraScrolledOverlayMaterialProgram.cpp
@@ -26,16 +26,16 @@ GXMaterialParameter GXCameraScrolledOverlayMaterialProgram::Parameters[9] = {
 
 GXCameraScrolledOverlayMaterialProgram::GXCameraScrolledOverlayMaterialProgram()
 {
+    Instance = this;
     programHash = 0x32BC21E8;
     parameterDataSize = 48;
     parameterCount = 9;
     glRegisterMaterialProgram(this, programHash);
-    Instance = this;
 }
 
 GXCameraScrolledOverlayMaterialProgram::~GXCameraScrolledOverlayMaterialProgram()
 {
-#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && !defined(MSCHARGED_GAME_MODULE)
     Instance = nullptr;
     Initialized = false;
 #endif
